  "title": "Scientist Warns Popular Children's Drinks Could Raise Blood Pressure Risk Later in Life",
  "summary": "A new long-term study suggests sugary drinks and excessive fruit juice consumption during childhood may increase the risk of high blood pressure in adulthood. Learn what the research found and why experts recommend healthier alternatives. Sugary drinks have long been linked to obesity, diabetes, and tooth decay. Now, new research suggests they may also increase the risk of developing high blood pressure later in life, especially when these beverages become a regular part of a child's diet. Res",
